{
  "Comment": "File-operations control plane. ONE machine serves copy, move and delete, branching on `operation` — the three share the request contract, the authorization question, the lock and the failure vocabulary, and a selection routes the same way whichever verb the user pressed. validate-authorize reads the trusted actor out of the API's identity block, authorizes the SOURCE and (for copy/move) the DESTINATION independently, confirms every selected item sits inside its root, refuses the portal's own folders per (side x operation), and emits the per-item outcome list every later verb carries forward. THE LOCK IS THE POINT OF THIS VERSION: FIFO orders DELIVERY per space, but the Pipe starts this machine FIRE_AND_FORGET and returns, so two operations in one space can run at once — and a delete removing objects a concurrent move has already relocated is silent, unrecoverable loss with versioning off. AcquireLock/LockAcquired/WaitForLock is a WAITING loop rather than a refusal, because this lock is per SPACE and covers all three operations: deleting a folder in alice/a/ and then copying one in alice/b/ is disjoint and safe, and refusing it out of band after the UI accepted the request would be worse than waiting. The waiter STEALS a stale lock itself, so its give-up bound is independent of the steal threshold; the give-up is strictly less than the machine's own ceiling, because the waiter is a state INSIDE the machine and the ceiling would otherwise kill it before its refusal could fire. THE CHOICE FAILS CLOSED: a third clause routes an acquire output that lost its shape to the give-up, because with only the two positive clauses it would satisfy neither, fall to the Default and SPIN until the ceiling — the one failure mode a loop has that a linear machine does not. THERE IS NO Validated PASS, AND ITS ABSENCE IS THE POINT: the neighbouring planes rebuild the whole state there to cross-check the verb's return shape, but three of this contract's fields are ABSENT for a delete (destination, onConflict and submittedAt are rejected for it), and a Pass reading an absent path raises an uncatchable States.Runtime — so the very first delete would die before NotifyFailure and tell the user nothing. StampExecution therefore MERGES the execution ARN with ResultPath instead of rebuilding, reading only $$.Execution.Id, which is always present. EVERY TASK RETRIES A TRANSIENT LAMBDA FAULT, the releases and the notifier included: a Catch is what stops a failed release failing the request, but a Retry is what makes the release actually happen — one throttle on ReleaseLock would otherwise leave the space locked until the stale steal, which is over three hours. THE UNKNOWN-OPERATION DEFAULT MERGES ITS ERROR RATHER THAN REPLACING THE STATE (Result + ResultPath, not Parameters), because it is the one seed reached while the lock is still HELD: a Pass that rebuilt the state would drop `$.lock`, and the release below it would then free nothing while reporting success. THREE RELEASE STATES, because one ASL state has one Next: the success path, the give-up and the failure path each need one, and the graph walk asserts no reachable terminal skips one. THE TOP-LEVEL TimeoutSeconds SHIPS WITH ITS RULE: AWS catchers cover Task, Parallel and Map states but NOT a top-level execution failure, so a timeout terminates the run outright with no state running and no Catch firing — the EventBridge TIMED_OUT rule (stepfunction.tf) is the second door into the same notifier, and it deliberately does NOT release the lock, because by the time it fires the lock may already have been stolen and releasing would clobber the new holder. TWO FAILURE SEEDS: the one for a failure that REPLACED the state seeds literal nulls, because the catch on validate-authorize has no object to merge into; the post-identity ones take the actor from `$.actor`, the verified username the validator already produced. Neither carries the forwarded request — RecordFailure reads it from the context object, rather than recovering it from a token. INSPECT-SOURCE EXPANDS ONCE AND WRITES A PLAN TO S3, and the plan is why ChooseOperation now routes all three operations to one state: a selection is a mix of files and folders, folders expand recursively into thousands of objects, and none of that can ride on a 256 KB state. The expansion is the same work for all three — what differs is only whether a destination is derived. NeedsDestinationGuard is a Choice on `operation` and NOT on the presence of `destination`, which is the trap this machine's own contract sets: validate-authorize normalises the copy/move-only fields to explicit NULLS for a delete, and IsPresent is TRUE for a field that is present and null — so the obvious guard would route every delete into a destination check it has no destination for. Its Default is the guard rather than the skip, so an operation that lost its shape reaches a verb that refuses it rather than one that writes. CHECK-DESTINATIONS REFUSES NOTHING WHOLESALE: a conflicted item comes back as an outcome record and every other item carries on, which is what the browser does today and what makes a select-all move survive one collision. BOTH NEW TASKS CARRY A Catch TO ReleaseLockOnFailure, and they are the states where forgetting one is invisible: a Task without a Catch has no edge to any terminal at all, so the graph walk that proves no path reaches a terminal holding the lock stays green while a fault there wedges the space until the stale steal, over three hours later. Each Task threads the running object via Payload.$=$ + OutputPath=$.Payload, so a verb that returned only its own fields would REPLACE the whole state — which is why every looping verb echoes what it was given. THE OUTCOME PRODUCER IS THE LAST STATE AND IT SITS AFTER THE RELEASE, ON BOTH OF ReleaseLock's EDGES: before the release it would hold the space for as long as the messages take to write, and a release that exhausts its Retry still has to reach it — otherwise an operation that COMPLETED tells the user nothing, and a browser waiting on that message to settle its in-flight record holds the space's submit gate until the ceiling. IT IS ALSO THE ONE TASK WHOSE CATCH GOES TO A TERMINAL RATHER THAN A RELEASE, and that is not an oversight: the lock is already free by then, a release is an OVERWRITE rather than a compare-and-set on the holder, and a second one would clobber whichever execution had since acquired it. ResultPath null on the state and on its Catch keeps the execution's output the terminal the finaliser shaped, and keeps a failed notification from becoming a failed operation — by the time it runs, a move has already deleted its sources.",
  "StartAt": "ValidateAuthorize",
  "TimeoutSeconds": ${state_machine_timeout_seconds},
  "States": {
    "ValidateAuthorize": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${validate_authorize_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "Next": "ValidateFailureSeed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "StampExecution"
    },

    "StampExecution": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Parameters": {
        "arn.$": "$$.Execution.Id",
        "name.$": "$$.Execution.Name"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.execution",
      "Next": "AcquireLock"
    },

    "AcquireLock": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${acquire_lock_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "LockAcquired"
    },

    "LockAcquired": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.lock.acquired", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.lock.acquired", "BooleanEquals": true }
          ],
          "Next": "ChooseOperation"
        },
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.lock.exhausted", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.lock.exhausted", "BooleanEquals": true }
          ],
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnGiveUp"
        },
        {
          "Variable": "$.lock.attempt",
          "IsPresent": false,
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnGiveUp"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "WaitForLock"
    },

    "WaitForLock": {
      "Type": "Wait",
      "Seconds": ${lock_wait_seconds},
      "Next": "AcquireLock"
    },

    "ChooseOperation": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "copy" }
          ],
          "Next": "InspectSource"
        },
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "move" }
          ],
          "Next": "InspectSource"
        },
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "delete" }
          ],
          "Next": "InspectSource"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "UnknownOperationSeed"
    },

    "InspectSource": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${inspect_source_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "NeedsDestinationGuard"
    },

    "NeedsDestinationGuard": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "delete" }
          ],
          "Next": "BuildTransferManifest"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "SeedFirstGuardPass"
    },

    "SeedFirstGuardPass": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Result": 1,
      "ResultPath": "$.guardPass",
      "Next": "CheckDestinations"
    },

    "CheckDestinations": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${check_destinations_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "SeedSecondGuardPass"
    },

    "SeedSecondGuardPass": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Result": 2,
      "ResultPath": "$.guardPass",
      "Next": "CheckDestinationsAgain"
    },

    "CheckDestinationsAgain": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${check_destinations_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "BuildTransferManifest"
    },

    "BuildTransferManifest": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${build_transfer_manifest_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "HasTransferItems"
    },

    "HasTransferItems": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.transfer.itemCount", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.transfer.itemCount", "NumericGreaterThan": 0 }
          ],
          "Next": "TransferObjects"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "CollectTransferResults"
    },

    "TransferObjects": {
      "Type": "Map",
      "ItemReader": {
        "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::s3:getObject",
        "ReaderConfig": {
          "InputType": "JSONL"
        },
        "Parameters": {
          "Bucket.$": "$.transfer.manifestBucket",
          "Key.$": "$.transfer.manifestKey"
        }
      },
      "ItemBatcher": {
        "MaxItemsPerBatch": ${transfer_max_items_per_batch},
        "BatchInput": {
          "traceparent.$": "$.traceparent",
          "requestId.$": "$.requestId"
        }
      },
      "MaxConcurrency": ${transfer_map_max_concurrency},
      "ToleratedFailurePercentage": 100,
      "ItemProcessor": {
        "ProcessorConfig": {
          "Mode": "DISTRIBUTED",
          "ExecutionType": "STANDARD"
        },
        "StartAt": "CopyObjects",
        "States": {
          "CopyObjects": {
            "Type": "Task",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
            "Parameters": {
              "FunctionName": "${copy_objects_function_arn}",
              "Payload.$": "$"
            },
            "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
            "Retry": [
              {
                "ErrorEquals": [
                  "Lambda.ServiceException",
                  "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
                  "Lambda.SdkClientException",
                  "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
                  "TransientError"
                ],
                "IntervalSeconds": 2,
                "MaxAttempts": 3,
                "BackoffRate": 2
              }
            ],
            "End": true
          }
        }
      },
      "ResultWriter": {
        "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::s3:putObject",
        "Parameters": {
          "Bucket.$": "$.transfer.resultsBucket",
          "Prefix.$": "$.transfer.resultsPrefix"
        }
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.mapRun",
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "CollectTransferResults"
    },

    "CollectTransferResults": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${collect_transfer_results_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "NeedsSourceDeletion"
    },

    "NeedsSourceDeletion": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "move" }
          ],
          "Next": "HasDeletableItems"
        },
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.operation", "StringEquals": "delete" }
          ],
          "Next": "HasDeletableItems"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "FinaliseOutcomes"
    },

    "HasDeletableItems": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "And": [
            { "Variable": "$.deletableCount", "IsPresent": true },
            { "Variable": "$.deletableCount", "NumericGreaterThan": 0 }
          ],
          "Next": "DeleteSource"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "FinaliseOutcomes"
    },

    "DeleteSource": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${delete_source_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "FinaliseOutcomes"
    },

    "FinaliseOutcomes": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${finalise_outcomes_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "OutputPath": "$.Payload",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException",
            "TransientError"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "ReleaseLock"
    },

    "ReleaseLock": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${release_lock_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "ResultPath": null,
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": null,
          "Next": "NotifyOutcomes"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "NotifyOutcomes"
    },

    "NotifyOutcomes": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${notify_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "ResultPath": null,
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": null,
          "Next": "Succeeded"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Succeeded"
    },

    "ReleaseLockOnGiveUp": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${release_lock_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "ResultPath": null,
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": null,
          "Next": "GiveUpFailureSeed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "GiveUpFailureSeed"
    },

    "ReleaseLockOnFailure": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${release_lock_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "ResultPath": null,
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": null,
          "Next": "RequestFailureSeed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "RequestFailureSeed"
    },

    "GiveUpFailureSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Parameters": {
        "traceparent.$": "$.traceparent",
        "requestId.$": "$.requestId",
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "error": {
          "Error": "lock_wait_exhausted",
          "Cause": "another operation held this space for longer than this request could wait"
        }
      },
      "Next": "RecordFailure"
    },

    "UnknownOperationSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Result": {
        "Error": "invalid_operation",
        "Cause": "the request named an operation this plane does not serve"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.error",
      "Next": "ReleaseLockOnFailure"
    },

    "RequestFailureSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Parameters": {
        "traceparent.$": "$.traceparent",
        "requestId.$": "$.requestId",
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "error.$": "$.error"
      },
      "Next": "RecordFailure"
    },

    "ValidateFailureSeed": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Parameters": {
        "traceparent": null,
        "requestId": null,
        "actor": null,
        "error.$": "$"
      },
      "Next": "RecordFailure"
    },

    "RecordFailure": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "Comment": "The single recorded-failure state every whole-request Catch reaches, after the lock has been released. Shapes the structured outcome { traceparent, requestId, actor, raw, status:'failed', error } that notify-failure reads, then fails the execution. It carries the RAW $.error {Error, Cause}, never a decoded reason: States.StringToJson raises an UNCATCHABLE States.Runtime whenever Cause is absent or is not JSON, which would kill the execution before it could record anything. Decode with cpcommon.errors.failure_reason, in Python. IT CARRIES THE FORWARDED REQUEST FROM THE CONTEXT OBJECT, $$.Execution.Input, not from the seed that reached it: a failure whose error REPLACED the state has no $.traceparent and no $.requestId left to read, and the envelope is the only surviving copy of the run — notify-failure parses the traceparent and the request id out of it in Python, which is the one place that value is reachable, since prising it out in ASL would need the banned States.StringToJson. Reading $$ here rather than threading it up through the seeds is also what keeps this to one key on one state per plane: the context object cannot be absent, so it is not a read any seed has to supply.",
      "Parameters": {
        "traceparent.$": "$.traceparent",
        "requestId.$": "$.requestId",
        "actor.$": "$.actor",
        "raw.$": "$$.Execution.Input",
        "status": "failed",
        "error.$": "$.error"
      },
      "Next": "NotifyFailure"
    },

    "NotifyFailure": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${notify_failure_function_arn}",
        "Payload.$": "$"
      },
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": [
            "Lambda.ServiceException",
            "Lambda.AWSLambdaException",
            "Lambda.SdkClientException",
            "Lambda.TooManyRequestsException"
          ],
          "IntervalSeconds": 2,
          "MaxAttempts": 3,
          "BackoffRate": 2
        }
      ],
      "ResultPath": null,
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.notifyError",
          "Next": "Failed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Failed"
    },

    "Succeeded": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    },

    "Failed": {
      "Type": "Fail"
    }
  }
}
